"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"[\\n {\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"K1006\\\",\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"When MLP depth/skips/activation/LN placement change, LN COUNT DOES NOT ORDER bundles, even at shared optimizer/lr/T. Do not turn pooled LN wins into an additive LN+residual score. q_172953 places residualSiLU then zeroLN residualReLU ahead of more-normalized rivals; q_07917a also favors zeroLN residualSiLU. Each is one10-seed-mean ordinal ranking,no loss margin. Old moreLN totals61/72 multivariate,57/69 univariate,41/45 tabular are confounded,NOT decision weights. Multivariate plain+1LN versus residual23/31(ratio.906),but full-config matches0 and+1depth4/9(1.166). Activation evidence K1008 cannot settle topology. Use exact-task/recipe controls.\\\",\\n  \\\"support_count\\\": 67.5,\\n  \\\"failure_count\\\": 43.5,\\n  \\\"credibility\\\": 0.6061946902654868,\\n  \\\"created_epoch\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"sources\\\": [],\\n  \\\"merged_from\\\": [\\n   \\\"K0002\\\",\\n   \\\"K0078\\\",\\n   \\\"K0268\\\",\\n   \\\"K0249\\\",\\n   \\\"K0256\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"origin\\\": \\\"seed:seed_distill_v1\\\",\\n  \\\"mechanism\\\": \\\"Observed LN effects are task/recipe-specific. No isolated causal residual=oneLN equivalence or universal normalization-first score is established.\\\",\\n  \\\"regime\\\": {\\n   \\\"family\\\": [\\n    \\\"univariate_regression\\\",\\n    \\\"multivariate_regression\\\",\\n    \\\"synthetic_tabular_classification\\\",\\n    \\\"xor_classification\\\",\\n    \\\"spiral_classification\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"model_type\\\": [\\n    \\\"mlp\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"note\\\": \\\"Shared optimizer/lr/T,lowDelta only. Check task-specific claims;LN count/residual/depth/activation are not additive units. Multivariate +1depth/matched-rate coverage limits K1076.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"phase\\\": \\\"Old moreLN counts and plain+1LN23/31 remain confounded;no additive score. Epoch11:q_07917a zeroLN residualSiLU C outranks normalized E/D/B at RMSprop/T1024;general advantage backtests2/8 vszeroLNrect,3/11 vsnormalizedSmooth;full-recipe lab20/80,no RMS matches. q_3bf8e9 also defeats forced residual/LN override. Ordinal counterexamples,not reverse rules.\\\",\\n  \\\"last_evaluated_epoch\\\": 14,\\n  \\\"report_ids\\\": [\\n   \\\"R04f88f629b\\\",\\n   \\\"R096205344f\\\",\\n   \\\"R69689e7876\\\"\\n  ]\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"K1018\\\",\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"XOR bundles with changed depth/skips/LN: smooth activation CANNOT order them. ONLY >=8features,shared Adam/AdamW/RMSprop lr/T,Delta>=.05 has a smooth-activation tendency (old lab15/16,CEratio.78;corpus6/6),not a sharp threshold or score. Excludes SGD/Adagrad,mixed optimizers,<8features. q_670f8a's plain rectifier beats smooth/normalized bundles (ordinal n10means,no margin). MoreLN,mixed architectures:36/51 high(37sets,.891),14/32 low(26sets,1.001);includesSGD/Adagrad. Fixed w24d2 plainGELU AdamW,T256/b16:2LN beats1LN atDelta.0256/.0512/.0768;high CE.67619/.68153. No validated fewer-LN reversal or additive ranking;depth K1065.\\\",\\n  \\\"support_count\\\": 15.25,\\n  \\\"failure_count\\\": 9.75,\\n  \\\"credibility\\\": 0.6018518518518519,\\n  \\\"created_epoch\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"sources\\\": [],\\n  \\\"merged_from\\\": [],\\n  \\\"origin\\\": \\\"c000005\\\",\\n  \\\"mechanism\\\": \\\"No sharp causal Delta threshold or universal LN reversal established. Fixed GELU AdamW favored two LN at all three rates; observational direction depends on selection.\\\",\\n  \\\"regime\\\": {\\n   \\\"family\\\": [\\n    \\\"xor_classification\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"model_type\\\": [\\n    \\\"mlp\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"data\\\": [\\n    \\\"1024rows\\\",\\n    \\\"8-16features\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"optimizer\\\": [\\n    \\\"Adam\\\",\\n    \\\"AdamW\\\",\\n    \\\"RMSprop\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"note\\\": \\\"Smooth:shared lr/T,Delta>=.05. LN audit includes SGD/Adagrad. Controlled w24,d2,GELU,AdamW,T256,bs16,one dataset,10 model seeds.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"phase\\\": \\\"Base-only moreLN: Delta<.05 14/32,26sets,ratio1.001324; >=.05 36/51,37sets,.891043. Mixed architecture at4096/8192 samples. Controlled Delta.0256 oneLN.692235/twoLN.692118; .0512 .687533/.684777; .0768 .681533/.676190. Older LN8/32 and33/41 filters underidentified.\\\",\\n  \\\"refines\\\": \\\"K1006\\\",\\n  \\\"last_evaluated_epoch\\\": 14,\\n  \\\"report_ids\\\": [\\n   \\\"R04f88f629b\\\",\\n   \\\"R096205344f\\\"\\n  ]\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"K1065\\\",\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"XOR >=8 features,shared optimizer/lr/T,Delta>=.05: depth/residual evidence is conditional,NOT 'depth helps only with residuals.' Older deeper-plain wins1/31 in13sets (CE x1.23); deeper-residual gap1-2 wins8/13 in7sets (ratio.82),not a default over shallow rivals; gap>=3 deeper0/4,corpus shallow2/3. Below .05 these penalties are OFF: deeper plain10/25,residual14/19. q_0eb782 at .03072 cannot be ranked by this claim. q_099d20's shallow residual beats deeper residuals but does not establish a full plain/residual ordering. Width,activation,LN and recipe confounds remain; do not transfer Adam-family observations to Adagrad/SGD without matched evidence.\\\",\\n  \\\"support_count\\\": 7.25,\\n  \\\"failure_count\\\": 6.75,\\n  \\\"credibility\\\": 0.515625,\\n  \\\"created_epoch\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"sources\\\": [],\\n  \\\"merged_from\\\": [],\\n  \\\"origin\\\": \\\"c000014\\\",\\n  \\\"regime\\\": {\\n   \\\"family\\\": [\\n    \\\"xor_classification\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"model_type\\\": [\\n    \\\"mlp\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"data\\\": [\\n    \\\"input_dim>=8\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"delta\\\": [\\n    0.05,\\n    1\\n   ],\\n   \\\"optimizer\\\": [\\n    \\\"Adam\\\",\\n    \\\"AdamW\\\",\\n    \\\"RMSprop\\\",\\n    \\\"Adagrad\\\",\\n    \\\"SGD\\\"\\n   ],\\n   \\\"depth\\\": [\\n    1,\\n    5\\n   ],\\n   \\\"note\\\": \\\"gap>=3 residual evidence is 1 lab set + 3 corpus pairs\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"phase\\\": \\\"\u0394\u22650.05: deeper plain 1/31; deeper residual gap1-2 8/13, gap\u22653 0/4 (+corpus shallow 2/3). \u0394<0.05: deeper plain 10/25, deeper residual 14/19.\\\",\\n  \\\"refines\\\": \\\"K1018\\\",\\n  \\\"last_evaluated_epoch\\\": 14,\\n  \\\"report_ids\\\": [\\n   \\\"R096205344f\\\"\\n  ]\\n }\\n]\\n\\n# R04f88f629b: Condition-first architecture claims: validated counts and counterexamples (0c676d9d5b42ccf0b715c62f8996ab9f0c124039)\\n# Condition-First Repair of Architecture Claims\\n\\n## Question and Sources\\n\\nInvestigated negative-utility K1006 (-0.07 n33), K1018 (-0.06 n52), K1009 (-0.06 n22), and K1038 (-0.03 n68), distinguishing retrieval/use mis-scope from factual failure. Independently validated `q_1f04dc` without requiring a causal mechanism.\\n\\nFrozen inputs: 863 history records and 11,215 base-lab candidates. A checkpoint refresh retained epoch-1 history and exposed current claim repairs plus experimental results. Base backtests exclude experiments; controlled results are reported separately.\\n\\nThe supplied utility estimates cannot be reconstructed from visible citations: K1006/K1018/K1009/K1038 appear in 16/3/1/1 cited records, respectively. Complete retrieval exposure and counterfactual utilities are unavailable. Negative utility therefore signals use risk, not necessarily false architecture facts.\\n\\nLab comparisons use held-out mean losses within one `set_id`. Excluded candidates are removed; nonexcluded partial-seed failures are retained for denominator reconstruction and separately tested. History supplies ordinal gold, not candidate loss magnitudes.\\n\\n## Definitions and Methods\\n\\nDepth counts hidden MLP blocks between projection and head. LN count refers to normalized hidden blocks. Residual addition is not defined as an LN-equivalent optimization unit.\\n\\nCalibrated \u0394 follows K1001/K1019: Adam/AdamW/RMSprop `lr*T`; Adagrad `2*lr*sqrt(T)`; SGD `lr*T*g/(1-m)`, using `g=.03` for momentum MSE regression and `.01` otherwise. This is a proxy, not measured parameter motion.\\n\\nThe scoped lab comparison requires plain MSE, a nonresidual candidate with exactly one additional LN versus a residual rival, \u0394 ratio 0.5\u20132, and the same set. Both \u0394 must be below 0.1 for the low regime. Equal width, depth, activation, or optimizer configuration is not required by the reported pooled fact.\\n\\nHistory backtesting requires equal optimizer type/lr and low \u0394. Ranked gold supplies eligible pair order; single-winner gold supplies order only when the winner belongs to the pair. The focal question is excluded from the historical backtest.\\n\\n## Validated LN-versus-Residual Fact\\n\\nThe reported lab result reproduces exactly:\\n\\n| Comparison | Plain higher-LN wins | Sets | Median MSE ratio |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\\n| Multivariate, both \u0394<0.1 | 23/31 | 25 | 0.906336 |\\n| Multivariate, at least one \u0394\u22650.1 | 5/13 | 12 | 1.054061 |\\n| Univariate, both \u0394<0.1 | 17/34 | 25 | 0.988537 |\\n\\nThe historical result also reproduces: excluding `q_1f04dc`, 40/52 wins across 31 questions; Adagrad 12/17 across nine questions. Including the focal case gives 41/53 and Adagrad 13/18. Thus the focal exclusion explains the denominator difference.\\n\\nIn `q_1f04dc`, A is plain depth2 width192 SiLU with two LN; B is residual depth1 width192 LeakyReLU with one LN. Both use Adagrad .001, decay .001, 256 steps, batch64, 16,384 samples, \u0394=.032. Gold A contradicts the solver\u2019s residual=one-LN tie followed by a rectifier tie-break. This directly demonstrates scoring misuse, not universal residual inferiority.\\n\\n## Stratification and Counterexamples\\n\\nLow multivariate lab evidence is concentrated at 4,096 samples: 22/30 wins, ratio .908. The remaining 8,192-sample pair wins. No eligible pair directly matches the focal 16,384-sample budget.\\n\\nEqual widths give 14/19 wins, ratio .889; plain-narrower comparisons 9/12, .924. No plain-wider comparisons exist. Input dimensions 2/3/5/8 give 3/3, 9/13, 8/11, and 3/4 wins.\\n\\nPlain-minus-residual depth gaps \u22121/0/+1/+2/+3 give 5/6, 7/8, 4/9, 2/2, and 5/6 wins. Crucially, the focal +1-depth subset has median ratio 1.166, opposing a depth-specific universal preference.\\n\\nEqual optimizer type/lr yields only 4/6 wins, ratio .913. No pair matches the full optimizer configuration. Equal-type AdamW gives 0/2, RMSprop 2/2, SGD 3/3. Mixed Adagrad-plain versus SGD-residual gives 1/4, ratio 1.119. These small, confounded strata do not establish optimizer-specific laws.\\n\\nRemoving every candidate with any failed seed changes low evidence to 22/30, ratio .898, and higher-\u0394 evidence to 3/10, ratio 1.076. Exact 23/31 requires retaining a nonexcluded partial-failure comparison.\\n\\nA 10,000-resample set-cluster bootstrap gives descriptive 95% ranges of .567\u2013.903 for win fraction and .721\u2013.959 for median ratio. These are sampling-sensitivity intervals, not causal guarantees.\\n\\nAll eight low-\u0394 losses remain recorded. Examples include `mvar_086f22` and `mvar_cf5f29`: plain depth5 SiLU three-LN loses to residual depth4 LeakyReLU two-LN at equal width256, with ratios 1.193 and 1.379. Optimizer decay differs. These counterexamples are not explained away.\\n\\n## Visible Retrieval/Use Records\\n\\nK1006 has direct scoring failures in `q_1f04dc` and conflicting residual/LN outcomes in `q_ca0dea`. Spiral and univariate records also challenge universal additive scoring. Their post-hoc mechanistic explanations are not treated as measurements.\\n\\nK1018 succeeds in `q_09e52b`: sixteen-feature XOR, Adam \u0394=.0768, smooth/fewer-LN winner. But `q_917f30` records a controlled counterexample near \u0394=.0512. Low-dimensional `q_a504f7` concerns residual overcredit outside the high-dimensional reversal condition.\\n\\nK1009\u2019s sole visible citation, `q_b0ae9d`, concerns low-\u0394 tabular ranking. Its missed comparison confounds width, activation, LN placement, and depth. It does not falsify the high-\u0394 aggregate.\\n\\nK1038\u2019s sole visible citation, `q_0e3752`, says the claim helped. The error concerned activation-versus-depth precedence in normalized residual regression, not zero-LN SGD. Relative held-out loss cannot demonstrate freezing.\\n\\n## Independent Scope Audit\\n\\nA separate base-lab audit uses plain MSE/CE and explicit same-set filters. XOR/tabular LN pairs match optimizer type/lr but leave architecture and remaining optimizer settings confounded.\\n\\nFor XOR with \u22658 features, more-LN wins 14/32 below \u0394=.05, ratio 1.001, versus 36/51 above it, ratio .891. No base high-\u0394 pair matches width, depth, activation, and residual simultaneously. The older 8/32 high and 33/41 low counts have an underidentified selection filter and do not reproduce under this explicit audit.\\n\\nHigh-\u0394 XOR more-LN outcomes vary by optimizer: Adam8/14, AdamW9/12, RMSprop10/14, Adagrad1/1, SGD8/10. Samples4096/8192 give 34/47 and 2/4. These observations do not establish an opposite universal LN rule.\\n\\nTabular high-\u0394 more-LN outcomes differ by data rule: piecewise9/17, ratio .987; smooth-additive5/13, 1.196; sparse-interaction0/10, 1.495. Below .1, corresponding wins are 38/56, 24/40, and 29/45. The pooled reversal does not describe piecewise boundaries reliably. High evidence covers 4,096/8,192 samples, with width/depth/activation/decay still confounded.\\n\\nFor SGD \u0394\u22653\u00d7 an adaptive rival with rival \u0394<.1, normalized SGD wins413/471, ratio .578; zero-LN68/119, .983; deep zero-LN11/30, 1.056. Deep plain SGD wins3/15, ratio1.897, versus residual8/15, .991. Regression gives5/21, spiral4/5, XOR2/4. Almost all deep cases use momentum .9; none are rectifiers. Width and sample-budget strata vary substantially. Older 21/60 and493/563 counts use different filters and must not share these denominators.\\n\\n## Preregistered Controlled Tests\\n\\nPredictions were saved before experiments. Only allowed lab datasets were used.\\n\\nOn `mvar_e57563`, fixed width96 depth1 GELU, Adagrad .001, decay0, 256 steps, batch16, \u0394=.032, residual and LN were crossed:\\n\\n| Architecture | Mean MSE | Seed SD |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| Plain, LN0 | .459344 | .007793 |\\n| Residual, LN0 | .451954 | .011002 |\\n| Plain, LN1 | .420702 | .010103 |\\n| Residual, LN1 | .419177 | .007300 |\\n\\nThe predicted plain-LN1 versus residual-LN0 preference holds: ratio .931, approximately 6.9% lower MSE. Equal-LN residual benefits are small. This supports one scoped comparison, not transfer to the focal target, depth, activation, or budget.\\n\\nOn sixteen-feature `xorcls_0dd7d2`, fixed width24 depth2 plain GELU AdamW, 256 steps and batch16, compare one versus two LN:\\n\\n| \u0394 | One-LN CE | Two-LN CE |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| .0256 | .692235 | .692118 |\\n| .0512 | .687533 | .684777 |\\n| .0768 | .681533 | .676190 |\\n\\nMore-LN wins all three means. The preregistered high-\u0394 fewer-LN prediction fails. The high-\u0394 ratio is .992; differences are small relative to seed SDs, and paired significance cannot be computed without seed-level covariance. No tested condition shows a sharp switch.\\n\\nCompeting explanations include architecture/optimizer selection, target-specific effects, and imperfect \u0394 calibration. The fixed XOR threshold prediction was tested and failed here. SGD freezing requires trajectories or initial-to-final measurements, which these rankings do not provide.\\n\\n## Repairs and Boundaries\\n\\nFour short, condition-first revisions were submitted for K1006/K1018/K1009/K1038. They remove residual=one-LN scoring, an automatic XOR LN switch, pooled tabular precedence, and \u201cnear-frozen\u201d SGD wording while retaining scoped counts, effects, and counterexamples.\\n\\nRefresh exposed K1076, but targeting it was rejected by the proposal snapshot. Its validated definitions and limitations were instead incorporated into K1006 without creating a duplicate claim.\\n\\nSolver precedence should first check family/data, loss, optimizer/calibrated \u0394, actual steps/sample budget, and comparable architecture. Scoped preferences must not override stronger evidence outside these gates. A counterexample limits a rule; it need not establish the opposite universal rule.\\n\\nUnresolved questions include exact replication of the focal 16,384-sample Adagrad configuration, matched LN-placement comparisons, transfer across targets, and SGD parameter trajectories. No causal theory is claimed.\\n\\n## Reproducibility and Publication\\n\\nSaved code, source records, candidate pairs, strata, predictions, controlled results, bootstrap specification, and accepted operations accompany `report.md`. Scripts compile and execute through the allowed lab Python interface.\\n\\nPublished report `R04f88f629b`; final repository commit `947b7c2b371af9f9267eaf4360f26857f5b88338`. Both controlled experiments completed.\\n\\n# R096205344f: q_b204a3: controlled XOR2 counterexamples and scoped surviving signs (9de8799df625fc5cb64298076ab835f9c01ccbd5)\\n# q_b204a3: Controlled XOR2 Falsification Audit\\n\\n## Finding\\nThe proposed interaction score is underspecified: it supplies no coefficients, thresholds or unique unseen-pair predictions. Its stronger operational interpretations are partly falsified. Extra LN can compensate for a deeper plain smooth stack, and deep residual smooth zeroLN need not be last.\\n\\nMatched rectifier, residual and terminal-LN mean preferences survive both tested splits, but some rectifier margins are tiny and uncertain. No evaluation ranking or scalar score was constructed.\\n\\n## Sources and Definitions\\nRead exact q_b204a3 and q_f74790, current K1006/K1018/K1039/K1065/K1133, and Refa052dfdc/Reb8454abdf. **K1039 is MSE-only; none of its counts or mechanism conjectures were exported to XOR CE.**\\n\\nThe focal hypothesis was formulated after revealing a bundled ordinal result. Its candidates vary depth, width, activation and LN placement, despite sharing SGD `.0003`, momentum0, weight decay `.001`, T256 and batch16. Numerical focal CE margins are unavailable.\\n\\nq_f74790 concerns XOR8 with Adam; K1133 uses a different normalized optimizer-comparison recipe. Refa052dfdc uses momentum SGD and different dimensions/batches; Reb8454abdf principally tests width24 SiLU on XOR4. These are context, not focal replications.\\n\\nDepth excludes the input projection. Blocks compute `act(Linear(LN(x)))`, adding `x` before activation when residual. Terminal LN normalizes the final hidden block\u2019s input, not the output-head features.\\n\\n## Preregistered Methods\\nSelected allowed XOR2 splits `12d3d2` and `13a317` before outcomes, excluding `076df5` already used by K1133. Each has standard-normal inputs, sign-disagreement labels, 1024 training and 2048 test rows. Freshness refers to new recipe measurements, not previously unused points.\\n\\nTested the complete factorial: depth2/4 \u00d7 plain/residual \u00d7 SiLU/GELU/LeakyReLU(.01) \u00d7 zero/terminal/allLN. Fixed width192, default PyTorch Linear initialization, linear two-logit head, plain CE, SGD `.0003`, momentum0, weight decay `.001`, T256, batch16, CPU, seeds0\u20139. Executable recipes are archived. Equal seeds do not ensure common minibatches across depths because initialization consumes RNG first.\\n\\nPreregistered predictions: P1 Leaky beats matched smooth activation; P2 residual beats matched plain; P3 terminalLN beats zeroLN for smooth stacks; P4 shallow plain terminalLN beats deep plain allLN; P5 every same-activation competitor beats each deep smooth zeroLN anchor. P4 explicitly tests a generalization, not the original bundled focal pair.\\n\\n## Focal-Excluded Backtest\\nExact-regime base-lab eligibility produced eight candidates in eight different sets: **zero within-set pairs**. History produced three eligible candidates in three separate records: **zero within-record pairs**. Thus there is no exact-regime historical validation denominator.\\n\\nAn exploratory `.0001\u2013.001` neighbor-history audit found 14 candidates across eight records. Registered P1/P2 comparisons came only from `q_0a0854`, at `.001`: P1 succeeded2/6 and P2 succeeded2/4. These match the full listed optimizer/budget but bundle architectures; there are zero isolated full-config pairs. P3/P4/P5 have no opportunities. Ordinal outcomes were not pooled with CE measurements. The focal comment\u2019s \u201c56 low-rate XOR records\u201d does not reproduce the exact eligibility filter.\\n\\n## Primary Phase Table\\nMean held-out CE, in nats. Entries are **zero/terminal/allLN**; P/R denote plain/residual.\\n\\n|Split|Depth|SiLU|GELU|Leaky(.01)|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|12d3d2|2P|.693617/.662568/.645833|.693330/.635356/.605868|.690400/.608791/.587019|\\n|12d3d2|2R|.685503/.653643/.620857|.668705/.617527/.563600|.656297/.608045/.555991|\\n|12d3d2|4P|.693499/.686890/.569930|.693496/.676784/.487288|.693342/.613922/.449651|\\n|12d3d2|4R|.683050/.623902/.490239|.647835/.563857/.386571|.602397/.545537/.384271|\\n|13a317|2P|.693582/.659811/.642129|.693270/.630782/.599828|.690122/.603273/.580411|\\n|13a317|2R|.683332/.648476/.614481|.664603/.609632/.554662|.652139/.600152/.546776|\\n|13a317|4P|.693467/.687508/.560986|.693465/.676613/.476723|.693343/.609089/.441415|\\n|13a317|4R|.682047/.619203/.479434|.644875/.557308/.377606|.598356/.539302/.376142|\\n\\n## Results and Uncertainty\\nPer split, mean-sign successes were P1 **24/24**, P2 **18/18**, P3 **8/8**, P4 **0/2**, and P5 **35/44**. These comparisons share anchors, seeds and datasets; they are not independent replications.\\n\\nDeep plain allLN minus shallow plain terminalLN:\\n- SiLU: **\u2212.092638**, paired95%CI[\u2212.116386,\u2212.068891]; **\u2212.098824**[\u2212.122559,\u2212.075090].\\n- GELU: **\u2212.148068**[\u2212.177678,\u2212.118458]; **\u2212.154059**[\u2212.183499,\u2212.124619].\\n\\nAll four contrasts favor the deeper allLN recipe in10/10 seeds, falsifying P4. Depth and LN change jointly in that contrast; the factorial retains the separating controls.\\n\\nDeep residual GELU zeroLN beats shallow residual GELU zeroLN by **\u2212.020871**[\u2212.035485,\u2212.006256] and **\u2212.019728**[\u2212.033841,\u2212.005614]. It also beats deep plain terminalLN on both splits. Deep smooth zeroLN therefore is not inevitably last.\\n\\nTiny margins remain visible: deep plain zeroLN Leaky-minus-GELU is **\u2212.000155**[\u2212.000582,+.000272],7/10 seed wins, and **\u2212.000122**[\u2212.000554,+.000310],3/10 wins. Favorable means do not establish uniformly strong rectifier advantage.\\n\\nThe exploratory depth4-plain activation\u00d7LN CE interaction, `(Leaky\u2212GELU at allLN)\u2212(Leaky\u2212GELU at zeroLN)`, is \u2212.037483[\u2212.042283,\u2212.032683] and \u2212.035186[\u2212.039730,\u2212.030642]. This is endpoint nonadditivity, not a mechanistic diagnosis.\\n\\nIntervals are unadjusted paired t9 intervals conditional on fixed data. They assume approximately normal independent seed differences, lack multiplicity correction, and do not quantify target-population uncertainty.\\n\\n## Rate Neighbor, Baseline and Failures\\nBefore boundary measurements, predicted that `.003` would preserve deep-allLN over shallow-terminalLN and deep-residual-zeroLN over deep-plain-zeroLN. Eight anchor configurations per split tested eight total contrasts. All eight succeeded in10/10 seeds, with negative paired intervals.\\n\\nAt `.003`, deep-all minus shallow-terminal margins were SiLU **\u2212.248173/\u2212.236504** and GELU **\u2212.172360/\u2212.167304**. Deep residual-minus-plain zeroLN margins were SiLU **\u2212.083965/\u2212.091759** and GELU **\u2212.264639/\u2212.275518**. No reversal appeared at this neighbor; no threshold was identified. XOR8 was unnecessary for falsifying the XOR2 assertion.\\n\\nCompleted **88 unique configurations,880 finite seed outcomes,zero failures/exclusions**, across two fixed splits. Cached receipt recovery added no replication. All264 measurement-file hashes and all88 curve endpoints were verified.\\n\\nStep0 CE is unavailable. Curves start after update1. Deep plain zeroLN SiLU changed `.69353385\u2192.69349851` and `.69347386\u2192.69346728`; GELU changed `.69353580\u2192.69349645` and `.69347636\u2192.69346549`. These tiny changes neither prove frozen features nor measure progress from initialization.\\n\\n## Mechanisms and Boundaries\\nRectification, LN geometry/affine capacity, initial logit calibration, activation-after-skip composition and finite-budget optimization remain competing explanations. No gradients, hidden RMS/Jacobians, actual updates or scalar-rescue diagnostics were measured. Endpoint interventions do not distinguish these mechanisms.\\n\\nConclusions are bounded to the tested width, initialization/head, decay, batch, budget, masks, activations and two XOR2 splits. Original focal mixed-width/placement recipes were not exactly replayed. No universal LN, residual, activation or optimizer law follows.\\n\\n**Unmeasured-setting prediction:** on allowed XOR2 `xorcls_17bdb0`, width256, otherwise identical SGD0 `.0003`/wd`.001`/T256/b16 settings, plain depth4 allLN will beat plain depth2 terminalLN for both SiLU and GELU in ten-seed mean CE. Either opposite mean sign rejects that transfer prediction.\\n\\n## Publication and Reproducibility\\nPublished before training, then published primary results and boundary predictions before boundary runs. Refresh pinned `Je8247e6fbbc4_research_e0010_v000001_90e2647e9082`; later inputs added no matched evidence changing the argument.\\n\\nArtifacts in `xor_audit/` retain frozen/checkpoint inputs, source reports, predictions, receipts, executable recipes, phase tables, paired statistics and backtests. Run `analyze.py`, `backtest_history.py`, `backtest_history_neighbor.py`, and `analyze_boundary.py` from the repository root.\\n\\nCorrections are retained: oversized snapshot replaced by gzip; rejected API overrides caused no training; analyzer/import issues were corrected. Preregistration misstated P5\u2019s denominator as22 rather than44 and boundary cells as ten rather than eight per split. Predicates and measurements were unchanged.\\n\\nSubmitted one scoped empirical KB addition for curation, without changing K1039\u2019s MSE scope or adding a mechanism/universal law.\\n\\nPublished **R096205344f**, commit `84093b6f9f8d69ddf01852d087653eada246e27b`. Independently reviewable evidence; unresolved mechanism and transfer boundaries.\\n\\n# R69689e7876: Target-dependent low-progress full-recipe reversals (2df9dece82c40a163735801c03a1f1ef7e77be76)\\n# Target-Dependent Low-Progress Full-Recipe Reversals\\n\\nPublished report **R69689e7876**, commit `2163bd7f8ce11fa0e3df0ceff2011e50662d4283`. Continuing investigation; the predictive mechanism remains unfinished.\\n\\n## Sources and Recipe Identity\\nRead K1006/K1008/K1076 and R04f88f629b first. Initial frozen inputs contained 1,013 history records and 13,141 allowed lab candidates. Historical evaluation answers were not used for experimental predictions. Checkpoint refresh pinned epoch e0008, version `Jc60aaee7d435_research_e0008_v000001_831a45b3c019`.\\n\\nBoth focal pairs have byte-identical choice sections, including optimizer, loss and default initialization, plus identical budget and evaluation sections. Choice-section SHA256 hashes:\\n- q_c692d1/q_1f04dc: `9cb7d53ff9b744ef5a7f3c16720aaa7cf4165d7f06b421e40cf22de9c692ba3d`.\\n- q_1e1b7e/q_c514ef: `d3b33ac31696bc8561cda2e717d4284fb73b61b4b6be961dc8cfc1385f5e1dab`.\\n\\nAll use 256 training and 256 test points, uniformly sampled on [0,1]. Targets and point seeds differ: 1972058668/1972050749 for the eight-dimensional pair; 1686238129/1686246048 for the four-dimensional pair. Thus historical reversals confound target with split and provide no numerical loss margins. Exact expressions and section hashes are saved.\\n\\n## Recipes and Intervention Limits\\nEight-dimensional recipes: A plain width192 depth2 SiLU, LN[1,1]; B residual width192 depth1 LeakyReLU(.01), LN[1]; C residual width256 depth1 LeakyReLU(.01), LN[0]. Shared Adagrad lr .001, decay .001, 256 steps, batch64, 16,384 samples, MSE.\\n\\nFour-dimensional recipes: A plain width192 depth4 SiLU, LN[0,0,1,0]; B residual width192 depth4 GELU, LN[0,1,0,0]; C plain width192 depth3 ReLU, LN[0,1,1]. Shared AdamW lr .00003, decay .00001, betas [.9,.95], 256 steps, batch16, 4,096 samples, MSE. Both panels use PyTorch defaults.\\n\\nCalibrated progress proxies are .032 and .00768, not measured parameter movement. The interface rejected dataset-level centering overrides; no documented centering/scaling intervention exists. These effects could not be isolated. Target shape, offset, scale and split remain confounded, alongside bundled LN/residual/activation/width/depth differences.\\n\\n## Predictions Before Measurement\\nInitial publication registered A<B on additive positive-baseline mvar_08cb38; B<A on oscillatory mvar_0fbae4; B<C on additive positive-baseline mvar_0c1000; C<B on oscillatory mvar_125029. \u201c<\u201d means lower mean test MSE.\\n\\nAfter mvar_0fbae4 failed, an additional B<A prediction on mixed oscillatory mvar_071e42 was published before measurement. The failed setting remains recorded. Predictions used target expressions, not candidate losses. Existing R04f88f629b controls were not repeated.\\n\\n## Results\\nMean test MSE, with lab-reported seed SD:\\n\\n| Target / Optimizer | A | B | C |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\\n| mvar_08cb38 / Adagrad | .344400 (.010089) | .536391 (.034137) | .635805 (.092013) |\\n| mvar_071e42 / Adagrad | .875571 (.019509) | .854737 (.013075) | 1.026673 (.044704) |\\n| mvar_0c1000 / AdamW | .660790 (.144905) | .303956 (.021717) | .428156 (.082361) |\\n| mvar_125029 / AdamW | 1.652787 (.017134) | 1.599238 (.027480) | 1.489847 (.078554) |\\n\\nEach completed cell has ten successful seeds, no exclusions and no cached measurements. All four completed preregistered pair directions hold. This selected panel does not estimate general predictive accuracy.\\n\\nAdagrad A\u2212B differences are \u2212.191991 and +.020834; A/B ratios .642068 and 1.024374. Same-label seed comparisons favor A in 10/10 and 1/10 respectively. AdamW B\u2212C differences are \u2212.124199 and +.109390; B/C ratios .709920 and 1.073424. Seed comparisons favor B in 10/10 and 1/10.\\n\\nDescriptive 20,000-resample seed-pair bootstrap 95% intervals, in that order: [\u2212.215799,\u2212.169434], [.009247,.035026], [\u2212.168335,\u2212.085581], [.059549,.165262]. Seed-difference SDs: .039819, .022038, .070985, .089335. These quantify initialization variability conditional on fixed datasets, not target/split generalization.\\n\\nFailure accounting: mvar_0fbae4 failed all ten seeds for each recipe, with excluded infinite summaries and zero-length curves. Finite returned terminal scalars were not ranked. Cause remains unresolved. Total: 150 attempted seeds, 120 successful, 30 failed. Its original prediction remains untested.\\n\\n## Interpretation and Competing Explanations\\nPreregistered numerical reversals occurred under identical executable recipes across completed target settings. The oscillatory Adagrad difference is substantially smaller than the additive difference. Neither LN count nor a universal residual override explains the conditional orders.\\n\\nBaseline fitting, feature propagation, activation/normalization interactions, complexity and split-specific approximation remain competing explanations. Centering causality was not measured. Successful directions do not identify the responsible target feature.\\n\\nDistinguishing tests require documented train-only centering/scaling on identical points, multiple splits per expression, and crossed architecture interventions. These remain proposed tests. Evidence is limited to the measured targets, fixed splits, focal optimizers and short budgets; no pooled scoring law is established.\\n\\n## Reproducibility and KB Updates\\nSaved answer-free source prompts, identity audits, requests, resolved specifications, every seed outcome, measurement paths/hashes and per-seed curves. Generated model/optimizer/loss/train files are byte-identical across completed datasets within each recipe panel. `analyze_results.py` successfully recomputed differences, ratios and uncertainty.\\n\\nSubmitted a scoped K1076 annotation and new AdamW full-recipe claim **K1123**, retaining K1006/K1008 without universal precedence. Full report and research artifacts are committed. The failed setting, centering/scaling limitation and need for an independent target panel remain unresolved.\"}],\"isError\":false}"